oint have to  deal with the American justice system  but that may not happen immediately  because Assange has unresolved business  with UK  first because you might recall and it's  been so many years at this point I mean  it's amazing all that's happened  politically while Julian Assange has  just been in the Ecuadorian Embassy but  back in 2012  Assange jumped UK bail so he faces up to  a year in prison in the UK and this  could just be the start of a very very  long process and the political  implications have gotten particularly  interesting because during the time that  Assange has been in the Ecuadorian  embassy we have now learned about the  connections between WikiLeaks to Russia  and the DNC and Hillary Clinton hacks  and the molar probe and the 2016  election everything that right now is  happening in terms of the UK bail  jumping and the 2017 sealed indictment  none of this stuff has anything to do  with Russia but you may recall from a  couple of weeks ago from the William Bar  letter about the Robert Moeller report  you may recall from my report six months  ago 12 months ago a year and a half ago  that during the time Assange was in the  Ecuadorian embassy now WikiLeaks  released tens of thousands of emails  that were stolen from the DNC and from  Hillary Clinton by Rutte but from the  Hillary Clinton campaign by Russia this  is part of Robert Muller's investigation  and as far as we were told by william  bars four-page letter to the extent that  we can believe it and hopefully soon  we'll have more specific information  about this wikileaks is also part of  Muller's report and when Assange went  into the embassy there was still the  idea or maybe the possibility that  wikileaks was not a partisan actor but  just a clearinghouse of information that  has drastically changed while Julian  Assange has been in the Ecuadorian  embassy we now know that WikiLeaks is a  part as an actor that's not a good or a  bad thing I want to be super clear that  people unde